    Map the opened lists to every encoded object
    
    The trusted planner now derives the positions each encoded object
    accumulates over the whole stage list: the folded message and a split Omega
    are opened by the shared test alone, Omega is also opened by every request's
    test, and a request's own objects are opened by its tests alone; main and mask
    objects keep separate counts. Each object's spent count is its opened list and
    its remaining capacity is the tail minus that list; the first object that does
    not fit is named with its gap, and no object's list is checked against
    another's count.
    
    This is the position-capacity mapping; the table, range and link hiding
    conditions and the whole-chain round budget remain the next steps.

